\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Crisis probability $p_{\mathrm  {crisis}}$ of the three regime detectors: changepoint detection (VIX, top), Hidden Markov Model (S\&P 500, middle) and clustering (Wasserstein k-means, S\&P 500 and VIX, bottom). Dashed: 0.5 threshold; grey shading: crisis periods; red lines: peak, trough and recovery.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pcrisis_sp}{{4}{8}{}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Monthly crisis probability $p_{\mathrm  {crisis}}$ of the three regime detectors: changepoint detection (VIX, top), clustering (Wasserstein k-means, S\&P 500 and VIX, middle) and Hidden Markov Model (S\&P 500, bottom). Value on the first trading day of each month, held until the next month, as read by the monthly rebalanced portfolios; it uses data up to the previous day. Dashed: 0.5 threshold, above which the portfolios switch to their crisis allocation. Grey shading: crisis periods from the S\&P~500 peak until it is back at the peak; vertical lines: peak, trough and recovery.}}{9}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pcrisis_monthly}{{5}{9}{}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {7}Portfolio Performance}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Crisis overview: duration and maximum drawdown (\%) within each crisis; baselines, monthly rebalancing. Trading Days: S\&P~500 trading days from the peak to the trough. Maximum drawdown: from the S\&P~500 peak until the S\&P~500 is back at that peak. GSPC: S\&P~500 price index.}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:crisis_overview}{{1}{10}{}{table.1}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Full-period performance 1998--2025; baselines, monthly rebalancing. Sharpe ratio on excess returns over the 3-month T-bill, annualised. CAGR: compound annual growth rate. Cum.\ return: cumulative return over the period. Ulcer index: root mean square drawdown from the running high. Turnover p.a.: average annual turnover, without the initial purchase. GSPC: S\&P~500 price index (without dividends), held buy \& hold; the portfolios are total-return series.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:full_period}{{2}{11}{}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Average crisis performance: equal-weighted average over the seven crises; baselines, monthly rebalancing. Fixed S\&P~500 windows: full crisis from the S\&P~500 peak until it is back at that peak, peak to trough, and trough to recovery (back at the peak). Max.\ drawdown and Ulcer index over the full crisis; cumulative return over each of the three windows. Recovery: trading days from the portfolio's own trough until it is back at its value on the S\&P~500 peak date, searched up to the next crisis peak; ≥: not recovered in at least one crisis (counted up to that cut-off, a lower bound); MCap and MVO did not recover from the Dotcom Crisis before the peak of the Financial Crisis (2007-10-09), so their Dotcom Crisis recovery is counted up to that date. GSPC: S\&P~500 price index; its full-crisis return is about zero by construction of the windows.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:crisis_average}{{3}{11}{}{table.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Regime detectors: changepoint (VIX), Hidden Markov Model (S\&P~500) and clustering (Wasserstein k-means, S\&P~500 and VIX), 1998--2025. Daily: the detector's own daily state. Monthly, quarterly, yearly: the state on the first trading day of the month, quarter or year, held until the next one, as the portfolios hold it. Episodes: number of switches into the crisis state; duration: their average length in trading days. Defensive: share of trading days in the crisis state. Entry lag: trading days from the S\&P~500 peak to the first crisis day (negative: already in the crisis state at the peak), over the crises entered before the trough. Exit lag: trading days from the S\&P~500 trough to the first calm day, over the crises in which the detector switches back. In brackets: number of the seven crises behind the average lag. Recall and precision per day against the crisis label S\&P~500 peak to trough.}}{12}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:detectors}{{4}{12}{}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {7.1}Crisis Excess Returns: Peak to Trough vs.\ Trough to Recovery}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Average crisis excess return over the benchmark per model: peak to trough ($x$) vs.\ trough to recovery ($y$). The dotted line marks $x + y = 0$: models above it gain over the whole crisis (peak to recovery), models below lose. The line is approximate, since the two phases compound, $(1+x)(1+y)-1 \ne  x+y$, rather than add.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scatter_crisis_excess}{{6}{13}{}{figure.6}{}}
